{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassEndomorphism.MassEndomorphismConjecture","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.MassEndomorphismConjecture","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.canonical","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassEndomorphism/MassEndomorphismConjecture.lean#L86-L120","doc":"**The all-zero model of `MassEndomorphism`.**  Every field is `0`:\n`q = 0`, `N = 0`, the coordinate family `z` is empty, and all three\ntraces vanish, so `vol_eq` is the arithmetic identity `0 = 0 - 0`.\nIt encodes no closed-form NF decomposition for any braid; it\nwitnesses only that the class is inhabitable.\n\n**A `def`, not an `instance`, since 2026-08-24.**  It was declared\n`instance` and its docstring called it *\"Faithful\"*, which it is\nnot — it is the zero model.  The defect was its **globality**: both\ncarriers are implicit (`{R : Type*} [CommRing R] {β : Type*}`), so\ntypeclass resolution supplied it for every commutative ring and\nevery braid type.  `fullMass`, `fullMass_eq_volume` and\n`braneTowerPartialSum` each take `[M : MassEndomorphism R β]`; with\nthe instance in scope those were not hypotheses, and\n`fullMass_eq_volume` proved `0 = 0` at every instantiation.  That is\nwhat §3b-tax forbids — *\"an unproved primary is honestly represented\nby a content-bearing class with **no** instance; do not fabricate a\ntrivial instance to 'close' it.\"*\n\nAs a `def` the zero model stays available to anyone who wants it\n(`letI := canonical (R := ℤ) (β := β)`) and nothing is discharged\nbehind a caller's back.  Blast radius of the demotion, measured:\n**zero** errors — the three in-file uses are binder positions, and\nno module outside `QOU/MassEndomorphism/` mentions the class.\n\nThe instance-free alternative for conditional work is\n`QOU.MassEndomorphism.VolumeBridge`, which ships no instance at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.braneTowerPartialSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.braneTowerPartialSum","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassEndomorphism/MassEndomorphismConjecture.lean#L78-L84","doc":"The brane-tower partial sum at level N, conditional on a\n`MassEndomorphism` instance.  Mirrors the\n`conj:brane-tower-z-habiro` Cauchy-sequence claim. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.fullMass_eq_volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.fullMass_eq_volume","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassEndomorphism/MassEndomorphismConjecture.lean#L68-L76","doc":"Conditional theorem: under the mass-endomorphism conjecture, the\nfull categorical mass equals the volume identity term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.fullMass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.fullMass","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassEndomorphism/MassEndomorphismConjecture.lean#L62-L66","doc":"The full categorical mass at brane-tower-saturation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.MassEndomorphism.vol_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.MassEndomorphism.vol_eq","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassEndomorphism/MassEndomorphismConjecture.lean#L60-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.MassEndomorphism.vol_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.MassEndomorphism.vol_identity","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassEndomorphism/MassEndomorphismConjecture.lean#L59-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.MassEndomorphism.tr_descended","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.MassEndomorphism.tr_descended","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassEndomorphism/MassEndomorphismConjecture.lean#L58-L58","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.MassEndomorphism.tr_transient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.MassEndomorphism.tr_transient","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassEndomorphism/MassEndomorphismConjecture.lean#L57-L57","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.MassEndomorphism.z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.MassEndomorphism.z","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassEndomorphism/MassEndomorphismConjecture.lean#L56-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.MassEndomorphism.N","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.MassEndomorphism.N","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassEndomorphism/MassEndomorphismConjecture.lean#L55-L55","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.MassEndomorphism.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.MassEndomorphism.q","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassEndomorphism/MassEndomorphismConjecture.lean#L54-L54","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.MassEndomorphism.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.MassEndomorphism.mk","kind":"ctor","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassEndomorphism/MassEndomorphismConjecture.lean#L53-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.MassEndomorphism","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.MassEndomorphism","kind":"class","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassEndomorphism/MassEndomorphismConjecture.lean#L34-L60","doc":"**The mass-endomorphism conjecture (axiomatised class).**\n\nA `MassEndomorphism R β` instance asserts the existence of a\nclosed-form NF decomposition for the Hecke mass element\nΦ_mass(β).  The fields encode the closed-form data:\n- `q : R` — the substrate parameter (in any commutative ring R\n  ⊇ ℤ[q^±1]).\n- `N : ℕ` — the number of brane levels.\n- `z : Fin N → R` — the algebraic-volume coordinates `z_i`.\n- `tr_transient : R` — `Σ Φ_q(z_i)`.\n- `tr_descended : R` — `tr_M(ρ(β))`.\n- `vol_identity : R` — the value `Vol(K_β)/ℏ_q²`.\n- `vol_eq` — the asserted equality\n  `tr_transient = vol_identity − tr_descended`.\n\nPolymorphic in the ground ring `R` (per\n`QOU.GroundRingAnnotations`, the formal-chain stub keeps `R`\nabstract; instances may specialise to `ℤ[q^±1]` or `ℝ`). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:mass-endomorphism","label":"conj:mass-endomorphism","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-endomorphism-conjecture.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}